  "id": "individualization",
  "term": "individualization",
  "definition": "Individualization is the process of tailoring a biomechanical model to a specific person by using that person’s measured joint and movement parameters instead of relying only on standard scaling methods. In this context, it is used to create a more personalized and accurate representation of the body during movement.",
